    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0558" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/1001: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Peck</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-06T15:00:00+08:00">February 6, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. McDaniel<anchor n="6" xml:id="d465-f1"/> was informed by Jabin Hsu,<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d465-f2"/> February 6, 11 a.m. that Suma<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d465-f3"/> has just told him that when in Shanghai February 5 he had
                    personally told Leith-Ross that in view of the imminent <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >rapprochement</hi> between Japan and China it would not be fitting for any
                    other nation to offer advice or otherwise intervene in China’s currency or
                    fiscal matters. Suma said he had called to tell Kung<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d465-f4"/> about this. However, Suma told Hsu the Japanese
                    Government does not disapprove of the recent bond conversion scheme and believes
                    there was nothing else for the Chinese Government to do.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Embassy and the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d465-f1" n="6" xml:id="d465-f1-content">
                <p>C. Yates McDaniel, Associated Press correspondent at Nanking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d465-f2" n="7" xml:id="d465-f2-content">
                <p>Director of General Affairs, Chinese Ministry of Finance.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d465-f3" n="8" xml:id="d465-f3-content">
                <p>Yakichiro Suma, First Secretary of the Japanese Embassy in China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d465-f4" n="9" xml:id="d465-f4-content">
                <p>H. H. Kung, Chinese Minister of Finance.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
